<article class="env-lemma" id="09BQ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09BQ">Lemma <span data-tag="09BQ">61.27.5</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a scheme. Let $\Lambda $ be a Noetherian ring. Let $K, L \in D_ c^-(X_{pro\text{-}\acute{e}tale}, \Lambda )$. Then $K \otimes _\Lambda ^\mathbf {L} L$ is in $D_ c^-(X_{pro\text{-}\acute{e}tale}, \Lambda )$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Note that $H^ i(K \otimes _\Lambda ^\mathbf {L} L)$ is the same as $H^ i(\tau _{\geq i - 1}K \otimes _\Lambda ^\mathbf {L} \tau _{\geq i - 1}L)$. Thus we may assume $K$ and $L$ are bounded. In this case we can apply Lemma <a href="/tag/09AL" data-tag="09AL">61.27.4</a> to reduce to the case of the étale site, see Étale Cohomology, Lemma <a href="/tag/0961" data-tag="0961">59.76.6</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>